      {
        "id": 70772,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-13T22:14:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah but that \"buff\" is insanely good. &nbsp;It is really hard to lose with a solid team and a TLT.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'm not saying that it's not incredibly beneficial and a huge game changer.&nbsp; I'm just saying that I'm one of the guys that prefers classic Tachyon.&nbsp; I like buffing my friends' hands, but I love utilizing my Burst cards.&nbsp; While it is an incredible bonus to the game to use Team Leader, I do want to note that it isn't strictly just \"better\" than Rapid Recon.&nbsp; Is it OP?&nbsp; Possibly. But it's different and a larger benefit to your entire team rather than an outright better power than Rapid Recon.&nbsp; It's a minor point, but I think it's one worth voicing.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
