      {
        "id": 70777,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-14T15:35:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I believe TLTach was designed to be more powerful. &nbsp;It is a Tachyon who survived Iron Legacy killing most of her allies. &nbsp;She's no longer a scientist moonlighting as a Super Hero to get funding, her split focus is gone and she is the toughened leader of the worlds only real chance at freedom.</p><p>TLT doesn't look out for herself nearly as well as the original, but she makes that team of largely replacement superheroes a viable fighting force.</p><p>The fact that Research Grant, the one card that is based on her role as a scientist is made obsolete is a phenomenal side effect.</p><p>No other hero gets an abilIty change that is a straight up boost to the teams chance to win and a health increase.</p><p>Tachyon leaves her job behind, gathers a new team and comes back stronger, focused on her team and determined to stop Iron Legacy, I love the story of TLT, which is why I allow her pretty much only when we are playing with freedom six cards or we've been horribly stomped and are out for revenge.</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:49:45.090Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
